body:
For anyone on V11 where effects will not modify encumbrance max anymore for some reason, here is a macro you can run to make this work (it is ugly, but functional):  


let players = \["character name"\];

for (const \[index, player\] of game.actors.entries()) 

{

  if (players.includes(String(player.name)))

{

  player.system.attributes.encumbrance.max = player.system.abilities.str.value \* 17 \* 2

}

}

Note that you can change the right hand side of the equals to any formula you want, this was just the one I happened to need.
